<h1>Format Labels</h1>
<hr align="left" width="100.526%" size="5" class="whs3">
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This command is accessible from</span> <b style="font-style:italic;"><i style="font-style:italic; font-weight:bold;"><span class="Path">Labels</span> &gt;</i></b> <i>Format</i> in <span class="Mode">Inspection</span> <span lang="EN-US">mode or from the</span> <b style="font-weight:normal;"><span class="Path">label context</span> menu</b> <span lang="EN-US">in</span> <span class="Mode">Edit label</span> <span lang="EN-US">mode.</span></p>
<p class="Description"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">This command calls the format dialog where you can customize what information to be displayed on the labels.</span></p>
<table class="TableGrid" style="border:none; border-collapse:separate; border-spacing:0px; left:0px; top:126px; width:757px;" width="757" cellspacing="0">
<col class="whs4">
<col class="whs5">
<tr>
<td valign="top" width="234" class="whs6">
<p><img src="../INSPECTION_MODE_FILES/format_labels.gif" width="201px" height="294px" border="0" class="img_whs7" alt=""></p>
</td>
<td valign="top" width="489" class="whs8">
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-US"><b>Name</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-US">Sets the name under which the label will be shown (this may be "Point" for example - then on the top of the labels you will see Point 0, Point 1...</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-US"><b>Font size</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-US">Sets the font size of the text</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Decimal places</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-US">Sets the number of the digits right of decimal point.</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-US">&gt;&gt; and &lt;&lt;</span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-US">Use the left (<b>&lt;&lt;</b>) and right (<b>&gt;&gt;</b>) arrows to show and hide the selected property (</span><span lang="EN-US" style="font-style:italic;"><i>X, Y, Z</i></span> <span lang="EN-US">- co-ordinates of the point, to which the label is assigned;</span> <span lang="EN-US" style="font-style:italic;"><i>Dx, Dy, Dz</i></span> <span lang="EN-US">- distances from the point to the reference surface projected on Ox, Oy, Oz axes respectively;</span> <span lang="EN-US" style="font-style:italic;"><i>D</i></span> <span lang="EN-US">- absolute distance from the point to the reference surface). All properties in the right column will be shown in the Label.</span></p>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
<p>If <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Format Labels</b></span> command called from main menu it affects all labels, if called from <a href="../User_Interface/Label_Context_Menu.htm">Labels Context Menu</a> it affects current label.</p>
